 the world and we can do  very well as a result of that the firing  of the neurone doesn't describe  something out there it's a response and  thought and language are exactly the  same they are responses higher level  closures as I would describe it so the  firing of the neurons a very low level  closure but we have a higher level  closures and those higher level closures  provide us with ways to intervene just  as the firing of the neuron provides us  with a way of intervening but let us not  imagine that that they somehow describe  some stuff which is utterly different  which is you know out there as it were  which I want to refer to as openness so  we're not tempted to think that it's  something in particular things are a  function of what we do with our closures  we make things to enable us to intervene  just one final thing why aren't we so  attached to this theological notion of  reality and I think there are a couple  of ways one one reason is because we  somehow think that if we give it up  anything goes we can make up any old  stuff and I don't think that's right we  can't make up any old stuff we have to  refine our closures we have to make them  better we have to make our tools work  better and we can be very very precise  about how we make the tools and I think  the other thing is we feel that we would  be lost we would somehow feel like the  medieval monks felt with the idea with  the arrival of the Enlightenment that  they'd have to give up the safety of  knowing where they are with God and I  think we just think no that's not right  instead if we give up on the idea of an  ultimate reality we have the potential  to create our ways of holding world  which are limitless and which give us  limb unlimited potential to intervene  and achieve things that we're not  achieving at the moment but let us not  imagine that any of them however  sophisticated they are are actually  somehow going to reach through human  concepts and human experience and touch  the world out there in some precise and  final way
 

